<Stub
  title="Indoor Playground & Open Play in Boise, ID | Bodies in Motion"
  description="Open play at Bodies in Motion in Boise, Idaho: a gigantic indoor play structure, four slides, free wifi and specialty coffee for parents."
  path="/open-play"
  h1="Open Play: The Funnest Indoor Playground in Boise"
  eyebrow="Indoor playground"
  showLocation
>
  <p>
    Walk in, grab a freshly brewed latte, find a cozy spot with free wifi, and watch your little ones unleash their
    energy on our gigantic play structure. Kids can ride four slides (the Vandal Vortex, Bronco Tsunami, Bengal Bolt and
    the Warrior Challenge), use imagination stations and a costume corner, and build with trains and Legos. Parents can
    also try pickleball while the kids play.
  </p>

  <h2>Open play cost</h2>
  <!-- TODO(Duncan): the old Pickleball page lists different open play prices (12-23 months $6, 2-4 yrs $9.60, 5 yrs & up $12, plus tax). Confirm which rates are current. -->
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li>12–23 months old: $8.25</li>
    <li>2–4 yrs old: $10.50</li>
    <li>5 yrs &amp; up: $12.50</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Monthly memberships for each child are $22/month (12–23 months), $28/month (2–4 years) and $33/month (5 and up).
    Annual passes are also available. Family monthly passes are $99/month and include all family members in the same
    household for pickleball, ropes course, and open play.
  </p>

  <h2>Hours</h2>
  <!-- TODO(Duncan): the old Open Play page shows "Summer hours" (Mon-Fri 9:30-6, Sat/Sun 9:30-5); the old Hours page shows fall and winter hours, used here. Confirm the current season. -->
  <p>
    Fall and winter hours for open play: Monday–Thursday 10 AM–7 PM, Friday 10 AM–6 PM, Saturday and Sunday
    9:30 AM–5:00 PM. <a href="/hours">See all hours</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Good to know</h2>
  <p>
    Due to food safety liability, outside food cannot be brought in. Snacks and drinks are available from Newton’s Cafe.
    Day cares and preschools can bring at least 10 kids for a guided Open Play field trip experience of 1½ hours;
    reservations are required.
  </p>
